# TKG & TAF (RAOS Ch.13–14)

Full docs: `docs/raos/chapter-13-*.md`, `chapter-14-*.md`.

## Travel Knowledge Graph

- Facts layer for country/city/season/festival/visa/transport/culture/safety/reservations.
- LLM must not invent festivals, blossom seasons, visa, tickets, travel rules — query TKG first.
- Source priority: government → tourism board → official attraction → transport operator → trusted partner → verified internal DB.
- Independent; do not write into Memory/DNA/Conversation/Decision directly.
- Updatable without rewriting AI architecture.

## Travel Agent Framework

- Task coordination layer: detect → queue → execute → validate → notify.
- Agents (Planner/Weather/Transport/Stay/Budget/Schedule/Reminder/Safety/…) share one framework.
- Continuous monitoring after trip creation; priority Critical → High → Medium → Low.
- User can accept / snooze / ignore / permanently disable reminder types.
- Agents collaborate (e.g. Weather → Schedule → Planner); **no major trip mutations without user confirmation**.
- Do not directly mutate Memory/DNA/Conversation.
